# Chain: Refactor

ID: RF1
Parent: D0

Purpose:
  The real duplication/debt-to-verified-refactor flow. Duplication surfaced
  by CR-XX (duplication_findings[], [R100]) and component-registry scans
  routes into this chain; each refactor is analyzed for impact, applied,
  tested, and verified. Replaces the auto-generated stub (Phase 152).

Owns: chains/refactor.sdd

Flow:
  DETECT -> AR -> RF -> TS -> QA -> VR

Stages:
  DETECT: Collect duplication/debt inputs — CR-XX duplication_findings[],
    component-registry scan (architecture/components.sdd), DRY violations
    flagged at BD/DS design time [R100].
  AR:  Analyze impact — which components/consumers are affected, blast
    radius, reversibility; decide extract-vs-extend per [R81]-[R83]
    (prefer reuse/specialization over duplication).
  RF:  Apply the refactor — extract shared component, extend existing
    concept, or remove the duplicate; update the component registry.
  TS:  Test the refactored surface — changed files only ([R76]); behavior
    preserved.
  QA:  Quality gate — no new CR findings on the refactored code.
  VR:  Verified — refactor proven complete with tests green.

Dependencies:
  AR  -> [DETECT]
  RF  -> [AR]
  TS  -> [RF]
  QA  -> [TS]
  VR  -> [QA]

Inputs (any of):
  - CR-XX duplication_findings[] (scoped reviews raise them)
  - BD/DS design-time reuse violations (component registry misses)
  - Human-raised debt (DEC-gated)

Routing:
  - DL1's scoped RF-XX steps are the PER-BRANCH instances of this chain
    (bax delivery.sdd RFScopedSemantics).
  - Chain-level RF1 handles cross-branch/cross-component duplication that
    no single branch's RF-XX covers.

Retry: 3

Navigation:
  Delivery: @delivery.sdd (RF-XX scoped instances)
  Stages: @../workflow/stages.sdd (CR duplication gate)
  StepKeys: @../workflow/step-keys.sdd (RF-XX canonical)
  Rules: @../PROJECT.sdd [R100]

State: +
  (Phase 152: replaced auto-generated stub with the real detect->verify
   refactor flow fed by CR-XX duplication_findings[] and the component
   registry scan.)
